course: dictionary
lesson: 8745
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings. The word serving is a good example. Read the words around it to find the right meaning. «From a shared dish you use the serving spoon and take a fair share.» The words shared dish and fair share tell you serving is about food.
explain: Sometimes the word is about work or a job. «The serving soldier stood guard at the gate.» A soldier who is serving is working in the army right now, so the words around it show which meaning is correct.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. If «a serving of soup» makes sense, serving means a portion of food. If the sentence still makes sense with a different meaning, check the clues again. A dictionary can show all the meanings.
fact: Serving can be a noun, a verb or an adjective.
fact: A serving is an amount of food for one person, also called a portion.
fact: Serving means giving food or drink to people, or working for someone.
fact: In tennis, serving is hitting the ball to start a point.
fact: Phrases include «per serving», «a serving spoon» and «a serving dish». «Per serving» tells you the amount for one portion, such as the calories on a food label.
exercise: A recipe «makes 6 servings». What does servings mean here? | Six plates to wash | *Portions of food for six people | Six pots of soup | Six cooks in a kitchen
exercise: «Use the serving spoon to take a fair share.» What is a serving spoon used for? | Washing up after dinner | Cutting bread | Stirring soup in a pan | *Taking food from a shared dish
exercise: «The serving soldier stood guard at the gate.» What does serving mean in this sentence? | *Working now in the army | Being very old | Bringing food to the table | Hitting a ball to start a point
test: In tennis, a player is serving. What is she doing? | Eating a snack on court | Sitting in the crowd | Giving a speech to her team | *Hitting the ball to start a point
test: A food label says «per serving». What does that mean? | The price for a whole family | The number of days the food lasts | The name of a cooking pot | *The amount for one portion
exam: A cook says «The recipe makes 4 servings.» How many portions is that? | Four plates to wash | *Four portions, one for each person | Forty people | Four spoons
